calized infection signs and high blast count", "Autoimmune disorders: insufficient evidence from current findings", "Metabolic decompensation: diabetes history alone doesn't explain constitutional signs or hematological abnormalities"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever 37.8°C, weight loss, night sweats)", "Acute neurological decline (20/100 visual acuity in both eyes, ataxia)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.12295567575848725, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The finding of blasts in peripheral blood with marrow failure strongly suggests a blast crisis (a phase of chronic myelogenous leukemia), which directly suppor…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.253277129203408, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The absence of T/B cell markers in blasts weakens lymphoid neoplasm as the primary diagnosis, as these markers are typically diagnostic for lymphoid malignanci…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute ly