ms are as follows:...\"\n  Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder: LR+=0.3333, LR-=1.1176 (Sn=0.05, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: small decrease → suggests weak_against]\n  De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia: [RAG context from Etiology of Acute Leukemia: A Review. > Clinical Significance]\n    \"Prognostic Assessment and Treatment Strategies...\"\n  Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis: LR+=0.0667, LR-=1.1647 (Sn=0.01, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: large/conclusive decrease → suggests strong_against]\n  Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML: LR+=4.6667, LR-=0.3529 (Sn=0.7, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: small increase → suggests weak_for]\n  De Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia: LR+=0.3333, LR-=1.1176 (Sn=0.05, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: small decrease → suggests weak_against]\n  Lymphoblastic Lymphoma: LR+=0.3333, LR-=1.1176 (Sn=0.05, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: small decrease → suggests weak_against]\n  Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia in Blast Crisis: LR+=0.0667, LR-=1.1647 (Sn=0.01, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: large/conclusive decrease → suggests strong_against]\n[LR Reference for 'Hypertension' (source: HPO)]\n  chronic myeloid leukemia: no data\n  polycythemia vera: LR+=1.79, LR-=0.21 (Sn=0.895, Sp=0.5, confidence=medium) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n  essential thrombocythemia: no data\n  primary myelofibrosis: LR+=0.3948, LR-=1.4576 (Sn=0.17, Sp=0.5694, confidence=medium) [EBM: small decrease → suggests weak_against]\n  acute lymphoblastic leukemia: no data\n[LR Reference for 'Anemia' (source: Guideline_common, RAG-context, RAG-quant:InternalMed_Harrison, RAG-quant:corpus, clinical_supplement:Harrison)]\n  Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase): LR+=0.3333, LR-=1.2857 (Sn=0.1, Sp=0.7, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: small decrease → suggests weak_against]\n  Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder: LR+=2.33